# Host-side secrets template for Docker Sandbox bootstrap.
#
# Copy to `.secrets` (gitignored — NEVER commit the real one) and fill in values.
# This file lives on your HOST and is used HOST-side to provision sandbox secrets.
# It is NOT read from inside a sandbox (gitignored files aren't in a clone/worktree);
# the helper reads it on the host and runs `sbx secret set`, so the token is injected
# at the proxy and never lands on the sandbox filesystem.
#
# Preferred alternative — skip this file entirely and set the secret globally once:
#   sbx secret set -g github -t "$(gh auth token)"
# Every future sandbox then inherits GitHub push with no per-sandbox step.

# GitHub token used for `git push` from sandboxes. Get one with `gh auth token`
# (or a fine-scoped PAT with just `repo` / `workflow`). Leave unset to have the
# helper fall back to `gh auth token` automatically.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
